{"metadata":{"accession":"PF00014","entry_id":null,"type":"domain","go_terms":null,"source_database":"pfam","member_databases":null,"integrated":"IPR002223","hierarchy":null,"name":{"name":"Kunitz/Bovine pancreatic trypsin inhibitor domain","short":"Kunitz_BPTI"},"description":[{"text":"<p>Indicative of a protease inhibitor, usually a serine protease inhibitor. Structure is a disulfide rich alpha+beta fold. BPTI (bovine pancreatic trypsin inhibitor) is an extensively studied model structure. Certain family members are similar to the tick anticoagulant peptide (TAP, [swissprot:P17726]). This is a highly selective inhibitor of factor Xa in the blood coagulation pathways [[cite:PUB00019765]]. TAP molecules are highly dipolar [[cite:PUB00019766]], and are arranged to form a twisted two- stranded antiparallel beta-sheet followed by an alpha helix [[cite:PUB00019765]].</p>","llm":false,"checked":false,"updated":false}],"wikipedia":[{"title":"Kunitz_domain","extract":"<p><b>Kunitz domains</b> are the active domains of proteins that inhibit the function of protein degrading enzymes or, more specifically, domains of Kunitz-type are protease inhibitors. They are relatively small with a length of about 50 to 60 amino acids and a molecular weight of 6 kDa. Examples of Kunitz-type protease inhibitors are aprotinin, Alzheimer's amyloid precursor protein (APP), and tissue factor pathway inhibitor (TFPI). Kunitz STI protease inhibitor, the trypsin inhibitor initially studied by Moses Kunitz, was extracted from soybeans.</p>","thumbnail":""}],"literature":{"PUB00019766":{"PMID":10716178,"ISBN":null,"volume":"9","issue":"2","year":2000,"title":"Structure of tick anticoagulant peptide at 1.6 A resolution complexed with bovine pancreatic trypsin inhibitor.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"265-72","medline_journal":"Protein Sci","ISO_journal":"Protein Sci.","authors":["St Charles R","Padmanabhan K","Arni RV","Padmanabhan KP","Tulinsky A."],"DOI_URL":"http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/picrender.fcgi?tool=EBI&pubmedid=10716178&action=stream&blobtype=pdf"},"PUB00019765":{"PMID":7925983,"ISBN":null,"volume":"352","issue":"2","year":1994,"title":"NMR solution structure of the recombinant tick anticoagulant protein (rTAP), a factor Xa inhibitor from the tick Ornithodoros moubata.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"251-7","medline_journal":"FEBS Lett","ISO_journal":"FEBS Lett.","authors":["Antuch W","Guntert P","Billeter M","Hawthorne T","Grossenbacher H","Wuthrich K."],"DOI_URL":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0014-5793(94)00941-4"}},"set_info":{"accession":"CL0894","name":"BPTI"},"overlaps_with":null,"counters":{"subfamilies":0,"domain_architectures":2835,"interactions":0,"matches":63106,"pathways":0,"proteins":32125,"proteomes":1457,"sets":1,"structural_models":{"alphafold":23680},"structures":229,"taxa":5145},"entry_annotations":{"hmm":0,"logo":0,"alignment:seed":98,"alignment:full":57813},"cross_references":{},"is_llm":false,"is_reviewed_llm":false,"is_updated_llm":false,"representative_structure":{"accession":"3t62","name":"Crystal structure of recombinant Kunitz Type serine protease Inhibitor-1 from the Caribbean Sea anemone Stichodactyla helianthus in complex with bovine chymotrypsin"}}}